[38;2;124;124;124m- $\int_0^\infty (\partial_r \psi_n)^2 r \, dr = \int_0^\infty 2^{2n} (\psi'(2^n[0m[38;2;124;124;124mr))^2 r \, dr$[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mLet $u = 2^n r$, so $r = u/2^n$, $dr = du/2^n$:[0m
[38;2;124;124;124m$= \int_0^\infty 2^{2n} (\psi'(u))^2 \cdot \frac{u}{2^n} \cdot \frac{du}{2^n} = [0m[38;2;124;124;124m\int_0^\infty (\psi'(u))^2 u \, du$[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mSo it's constant, doesn't go to $0$.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mThe issue is that the weight $r \, dr$ is not scale-invariant in a way that [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mhelps. Let me think about what $f_n$ could do.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mWe want $\int_0^\infty (\psi'(f_n(r)))^2 (f_n'(r))^2 r \, dr \to 0$.[0m

